{"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Standard Library"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Preserving the Results of a Throwing Expression"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Call the initializer that wraps a throwing expression when you need to serialize"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or memoize the result."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/preserving-the-results-of-a-throwing-expression"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/preserving-the-results-of-a-throwing-expression"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/numbers-and-basic-values","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sometimes you need to preserve the entire result of a function call or other expression"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that can either throw or return a value. For example, you may need to serialize the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"result or pass it as a value to another part of your app that handles the result"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"data. Use the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result"},{"type":"text","text":" type in these scenarios to capture the result of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"potentially failing operation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Identify a Throwing Expression to Preserve","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Identify-a-Throwing-Expression-to-Preserve"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Typically, you use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"do-catch"},{"type":"text","text":" statements to handle throwing expressions immediately,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but sometimes you need to store the whole result of the operation for later processing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"during tasks like analyzing a batch of calls. The following example introduces an","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API that generates random numbers, but that fails approximately half of the time."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["enum EntropyError: Error {","    case entropyDepleted","}","","struct UnreliableRandomGenerator {","    func random() throws -> Int {","        if Bool.random() {","            return Int.random(in: 1...100)","        } else {","            throw EntropyError.entropyDepleted","        }","    }","}"]},{"text":"Convert the Throwing Expression to a Result","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Convert-the-Throwing-Expression-to-a-Result"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You preserve the return value or thrown error from a throwing expression using the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result"},{"text":" enumeration’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result\/init(catching:)-62kyq"},{"text":" initializer. Invoke","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the throwing expression inside the closure you pass to the initializer:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let singleSample = Result { try UnreliableRandomGenerator().random() }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In most scenarios, you use the preserved result as part of broader functionality","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in your code. For example, you may run a series of randomness tests and compute the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"statistical average of both a range of numbers returned from a random number generator,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as well as the failure rate of calling the API. In these cases, you need to store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the whole result rather than just the success value or that the API call failed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example uses the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result\/init(catching:)-62kyq","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" initializer in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"broader context of saving a series of calls for later statistical analysis:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct RandomnessMonitor {","    let randomnessSource: UnreliableRandomGenerator","    var results: [Result<Int, Error>] = []","","    init(generator: UnreliableRandomGenerator) {","        randomnessSource = generator","    }","","    mutating func sample() {","        let sample = Result { try randomnessSource.random() }","        results.append(sample)","    }","","    func summary() -> (Double, Double) {","        let totals = results.reduce((sum: 0, count: 0)) { total, sample in","            switch sample {","            case .success(let number):","                return (total.sum + number, total.count)","            case .failure:","                return (total.sum, total.count + 1)","            }","        }","","        return (","            average: Double(totals.sum) \/ Double(results.count - totals.count),","            failureRate: Double(totals.count) \/ Double(results.count)","        )","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Running the analysis on a sufficiently large sample generates an average number near","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"50 and a failure rate near 50%:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var monitor = RandomnessMonitor(generator: UnreliableRandomGenerator())","(0..<1000).forEach { _ in monitor.sample() }","let (average, failureRate) = monitor.summary()","print(\"Average value: \\(average), failure rate: \\(failureRate * 100.0)%.\")","\/\/ Prints values such as: \"Average value: 47.95, failure rate: 48.69%.\""]}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result\/init(catching:)-62kyq"],"anchor":"Converting-a-Throwing-Expression-to-a-Result","generated":true,"title":"Converting a Throwing Expression to a Result"}],"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","role":"collection","title":"Standard Library","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Standard Library","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swift","abstract":[{"text":"Browse the essential types provided by Swift’s standard library.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/numbers-and-basic-values":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/numbers-and-basic-values","role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/numbers-and-basic-values","title":"Numbers and Basic Values","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Model data with numbers, Boolean values, and other fundamental types."}]},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/Result":{"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/result","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Result","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result","title":"Result","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Result","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A value that represents either a success or a failure, including an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"associated value in each case."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/Result/init(catching:)-62kyq":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"catching","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": () ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s6ResultOsRi_zrlE7Failureq_mfp","text":"Failure","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s6ResultOsRi_zrlE7Successxmfp","text":"Success","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Failure"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/result\/init(catching:)-62kyq","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new result by evaluating a throwing closure, capturing the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returned value as a success, or any thrown error as a failure."}],"role":"symbol","title":"init(catching:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Result\/init(catching:)-62kyq"}}}